the maximum capacity and the current population. Which differential equation models this population?" :question/worked-solution "The rate at which the number of cultures $B(t)$ in the laboratory incubator changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum capacity and the current number of cultures. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-B),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum capacity, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=452$ cultures, and $k=5$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=5(452-B).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["7875e0a1-7a16-5786-87e7-5a77a72087b1"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "37e6c9ed-bf02-5ef5-8c5a-02b0b5c319c5" :answer/id #uuid "37e6c9ed-bf02-5ef5-8c5a-02b0b5c319c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=-2(88-C)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "563e8011-b5e6-5788-9e23-b206633aecb5" :answer/id #uuid "563e8011-b5e6-5788-9e23-b206633aecb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=2(33-C)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "74d8e960-6bba-58e5-b08e-581702e7a76c" :answer/id #uuid "74d8e960-6bba-58e5-b08e-581702e7a76c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=176-C" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4bd1d390-d8de-540e-9210-b415fa61cff9" :answer/id #uuid "4bd1d390-d8de-540e-9210-b415fa61cff9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=2(88-C)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2be091ba-6bb6-5883-8103-314cd3df15d4" :answer/id #uuid "2be091ba-6bb6-5883-8103-314cd3df15d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=(88-C)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6211314d-6f8c-5806-9551-2e82c0125d2d" :answer-field/id #uuid "6211314d-6f8c-5806-9551-2e82c0125d2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["37e6c9ed-bf02-5ef5-8c5a-02b0b5c319c5" "563e8011-b5e6-5788-9e23-b206633aecb5" "74d8e960-6bba-58e5-b08e-581702e7a76c" "4bd1d390-d8de-540e-9210-b415fa61cff9" "2be091ba-6bb6-5883-8103-314cd3df15d4"] :answer-field/correct "4bd1d390-d8de-540e-9210-b415fa61cff9" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "6fe2e758-0b83-5e24-b0e9-a0f44f5d812a" :question/id #uuid "6fe2e758-0b83-5e24-b0e9-a0f44f5d812a" :question/problem "A data center initially contains $33$ computers, and its maximum capacity is $88$ computers. Let $C(t)$ be the number of computers, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time in months. Its population obeys an inhibited growth model. The rate of increase equals $2$ times the difference between the maximum capacity and the current population. Which differential equation models this population?" :question/worked-solution "The rate at which the number of computers $C(t)$ in the data center changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum capacity and the current number of computers. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-C),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum capacity, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=88$ computers, and $k=2$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=2(88-C).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["6211314d-6f8c-5806-9551-2e82c0125d2d"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "6433720d-0437-5761-a06c-4f51d076ab3f" :answer/id #uuid "6433720d-0437-5761-a06c-4f51d076ab3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-2(461-N)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fa19b207-aa8e-51a1-a052-84f0fcf25190" :answer/id #uuid "fa19b207-aa8e-51a1-a052-84f0fcf25190" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=(461-N)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "41f9afda-dab8-5ea1-a543-78cd7ef01897" :answer/id #uuid "41f9afda-dab8-5ea1-a543-7