text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=2(461-N).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["7c7b268c-acbe-5154-8908-9ef519371ae4"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "92134b70-81f2-514e-a9ea-7ac07ec43bee" :answer/id #uuid "92134b70-81f2-514e-a9ea-7ac07ec43bee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=6(141-C)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1d486b04-f058-5b0f-bf81-6de58ef21030" :answer/id #uuid "1d486b04-f058-5b0f-bf81-6de58ef21030" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=-6(141-C)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d6493761-babb-5f3f-92ed-987fa217746f" :answer/id #uuid "d6493761-babb-5f3f-92ed-987fa217746f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=6(34-C)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "97cd59c6-fe5e-5a8b-8a3e-b641e19282e0" :answer/id #uuid "97cd59c6-fe5e-5a8b-8a3e-b641e19282e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=846-C" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "bb66c481-6441-50e6-9df5-076fb8d43fe2" :answer/id #uuid "bb66c481-6441-50e6-9df5-076fb8d43fe2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=(141-C)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fd1be51c-0b3a-58b7-b967-cde05f295d58" :answer-field/id #uuid "fd1be51c-0b3a-58b7-b967-cde05f295d58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["92134b70-81f2-514e-a9ea-7ac07ec43bee" "1d486b04-f058-5b0f-bf81-6de58ef21030" "d6493761-babb-5f3f-92ed-987fa217746f" "97cd59c6-fe5e-5a8b-8a3e-b641e19282e0" "bb66c481-6441-50e6-9df5-076fb8d43fe2"] :answer-field/correct "92134b70-81f2-514e-a9ea-7ac07ec43bee" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "77765534-844a-550d-9d04-0aee6519495b" :question/id #uuid "77765534-844a-550d-9d04-0aee6519495b" :question/problem "A data center initially contains $34$ computers, and its maximum capacity is $141$ computers. Let $C(t)$ be the number of computers, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time in months. Its population obeys an inhibited growth model. The rate of increase equals $6$ times the difference between the maximum capacity and the current population. Which differential equation models this population?" :question/worked-solution "The rate at which the number of computers $C(t)$ in the data center changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum capacity and the current number of computers. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-C),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum capacity, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=141$ computers, and $k=6$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=6(141-C).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["fd1be51c-0b3a-58b7-b967-cde05f295d58"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "16ca42ad-233a-5895-8bd3-844ba110ab51" :answer/id #uuid "16ca42ad-233a-5895-8bd3-844ba110ab51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=2(102-M)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "94565dab-5616-5a0e-8dd7-c18b93bea82b" :answer/id #uuid "94565dab-5616-5a0e-8dd7-c18b93bea82b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=280-M" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1c04a060-138f-59f7-b590-fdbeca98fb18" :answer/id #uuid "1c04a060-138f-59f7-b590-fdbeca98fb18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=2(140-M)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "319ab441-06a9-5ffb-a6ea-7c0edcb3f112" :answer/id #uuid "319ab441-06a9-5ffb-a6ea-7c0edcb3f112" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=-2(140-M)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ae81661e-4cd7-5065-ac1c-341ae0905ff2" :answer/id #uuid "ae81661e-4cd7-5065-ac1c-341ae0905ff2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=(140-M)" :db/ensure :answer/v